provider_responses.text:
The key clarification is:

> **“No upfront payment” only describes the cost of starting registration. It does not guarantee that every user, signup route, or later feature has no financial or document requirements.**

To make this actionable, show users:

- the exact signup route they are using;
- documents required for their user type;
- whether an initial transfer is required and whether it remains their money;
- any fees that can occur later;
- what happens if digital verification fails;
- that approval depends on review, not just document submission.

Use plain language and label each requirement as either **required to apply**, **required to activate**, or **optional after signup**.

